.TH update "" "Administration"
.SH NAME
update \- periodically flush file system buffers to disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB/etc/update\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
update -- flush file system buffers periodically
Usage:	/etc/update
update calls sync every 30 seconds, forever.
It ignores the interrupt and hangup signals.
.HE
.B update
runs forever, calling
.B sync()
every 30 seconds to flush modified in-memory disk buffers out to disk.
It takes no arguments and recognizes no options.
.PP
.B update
ignores both the interrupt
.RB ( SIGINT )
and hangup
.RB ( SIGHUP )
signals, so that it cannot be killed by a signal from its controlling
terminal.
It is normally started once, from
.BR /etc/rc ,
and left running in the background for the life of the system.
.SH FILES
.B /etc/update
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sync ,
.B sync()
.SH NOTES
There is no entry for
.B update
in
.BR /etc/helpfile ;
the summary above is written from the source.
